<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burchard of Worms</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 965–1025</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burchard of Worms was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Worms from 1000 to 1025. Between about 1008 and 1012 he compiled the Decretum, a collection of canon law in twenty books that became the standard handbook of church law until Gratian in the 12th century. He also issued a law code for the dependants of his church and strengthened the bishop's authority over the city of Worms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burchard-of-worms.jpg" alt="Burchard of Worms" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heidas Wikipedia account All pictures Please use this discussion page · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Worms_Doom_2005-05-27b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
